    "updated_at": "2022-06-02T10:11:42Z",
    "body": "I think this is a good idea, but podman doesn't guarantee that name is anything useful.  If you're using Toolbox then it's fine, it'll reflect the toolbox name.  If you run an image without specifying a name via the \"podman run --name=FakeName\" option to then it generates a random name:\r\n```bash\r\n└> podman run -d -p 8080:80 nginx\r\nfb7bc945f279ff1a9f60dbdc5dd551fba57121073516dd3dd9eec806e5b26d5e\r\n└> podman ps\r\nCONTAINER ID  IMAGE                   COMMAND               CREATED        STATUS            PORTS                 NAMES\r\nfb7bc945f279  localhost/nginx:latest  nginx -g daemon o...  7 seconds ago  Up 7 seconds ago  0.0.0.0:8080->80/tcp  zen_elgamal\r\n```\r\n\r\nI guess that's why the original implementation is as it is, but I think we should expose both, name as \"name\" and the current implementation as \"container_image\" or something similar.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
