    "updated_at": "2022-11-20T12:48:32Z",
    "body": "Just wanted to say I may have a similar problem with [Distrobox](https://distrobox.privatedns.org/) containers.\r\n\r\nCurrently, it displays `Systemd` as the container name (using Podman backend) while I expect to have the `name` value from `/run/.containerenv`.\r\n\r\nBut maybe there is another bug because if I had the env's image name displayed as the container name in Starship, I whould have `docker.io/library/ubuntu:22.04` for example (because the value of `image` in `/run/.containerenv` is not `Systemd` but the name of the image).",
