    "updated_at": "2022-11-20T16:01:28Z",
    "body": "> Just wanted to say I may have a similar problem with [Distrobox](https://distrobox.privatedns.org/) containers.\r\n> \r\n> Currently, it displays `Systemd` as the container name (using Podman backend) while I expect to have the `name` value from `/run/.containerenv`.\r\n> \r\n> But maybe there is another bug because if I had the env's image name displayed as the container name in Starship, I whould have `docker.io/library/ubuntu:22.04` for example (because the value of `image` in `/run/.containerenv` is not `Systemd` but the name of the image).\r\n\r\nHey @sambonbonne - I actually know why this is happening, as I found it while looking at PRing a fix for this, the order in which Starship checks for the \"name\" here prioritizes the `systemd` based branch. I'm not familiar enough with `systemd` based containerization to know a better/more fair determination but a naive fix would be moving [this block](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/modules/container.rs#L29-L39) to after the check for podman. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
