    "updated_at": "2022-11-21T08:58:47Z",
    "body": "Thanks @spencergilbert for finding this!\r\n\r\nIt's even funny to `return Some(\"Systemd\".into());` instead of returning the content of the file (which is `docker` for my two distroboxes). \r\nI also don't know a lot about systemd containers so maybe the content of this file is not really something useful.\r\n\r\nAnd I don't really understand why Distrobox set theses variables as I use Distrobox with Podman (and the other possible engine is Docker but I checked, it's not the one I use despite the `docker` value in the systemd's file).\r\n\r\nLike you, I think the `/run/.containerenv` file should be checked first but I don't know if it wouldn't break anything for existing users relying on this behavior.",
